'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  test-contract-gaps-p4-rep-skipf.spin2
''   Purpose....  Whether REP nests, and what SKIPF does in hub execution,
''                arms R and S.  No pins are used.
''   Manual.....  P2 Knowledge Base
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Nov 2026
''   Updated....  Nov 2026
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz, NOTHING attached.  No pins are touched.
  Build pnut-ts -d.  Cog 0 supervises and prints; no other cog has the
  debugger.  Every run is one fresh worker cog; the supervisor stops a worker
  that has not finished in its limit and reports the run as not finished, so
  no step can hang the program.  Results print before verdicts, and every
  reading not named below is printed raw.

ARM R  What happens when a REP block contains another REP?
  The P2 Documentation describes one REP at a time and says a branch inside
  the block cancels it; it does not say what a second REP does.  The block
  runs in cog RAM, once per case and per repeat:
      site O: REP #5,#5  or NOP
              ADD pre,#1            outer body 1
      site I: REP #2,#3  or NOP     outer body 2
              ADD in1,#1            outer body 3, inner body 1
              ADD in2,#1            outer body 4, inner body 2
              ADD post,#1           outer body 5
  The two sites are patched in cog RAM before the block runs, so the three
  cases differ only in those two words.
    Control      outer only (site I is a NOP): every counter 5.
    Control      inner only (site O is a NOP): pre 1, in1 3, in2 3, post 1.
    Premise      the site words read back from cog RAM after the run are the
                 words the case needs; in the case under test pre and in1 are
                 at least 1, so the block reached the inner REP's slot and went
                 past it.  The outer-only control shows the outer REP spans
                 that slot; the inner-only control shows the same word in the
                 same slot works as a REP.
    Measure      both REPs in place, three repeats.

  READINGS, every repeat of the case under test must agree:
    NESTS            pre 5, in1 15, in2 15, post 5
    INNER REPLACES   pre 1, in1 3, in2 3, post 1; the outer REP is gone
    INNER IGNORED    pre 5, in1 5, in2 5, post 5; the inner REP did nothing
    BOTH CANCELLED   pre 1, in1 1, in2 1, post 1; neither repeated
    OTHER            one other set of counts, printed raw
    MIXED            the repeats did not agree; the run lines are the raw values
    NO READING       a premise or a control above missed, or a run did not finish

ARM S  What does SKIPF do in hub execution?
  The instruction table marks SKIPF illegal in hub execution.  The P2
  Documentation says it reverts to SKIP, cancelling instructions in the
  pipeline instead of stepping over them.  The body is one site and nine ADDs
  of weights 1 to 256; the sum says exactly which ADDs ran, and two GETCTs
  time the site and the ADDs.  The body exists once in cog RAM and once in hub
  RAM, and the site is patched to SKIP or SKIPF before the body runs, so each
  body runs both instructions at one address.  Pattern %1011_1110: the first,
  seventh and ninth ADDs run, sum 321.  Pattern 0: all nine run, sum 511.
    Control      cog SKIP, pattern: sum 321.
    Control      cog SKIPF, pattern: sum 321, and fewer clocks than cog SKIP.
                 Six instructions are stepped over, so the difference is the
                 clocks a leap saves; it must exceed twice S_TOL or the time
                 cannot separate the two readings.
    Control      cog SKIPF, pattern 0: sum 511.
    Control      hub SKIP, pattern: sum 321, and the five times agree to within
                 S_TOL.
    Control      hub SKIP, pattern 0: sum 511.
    Premise      every run captures its own PC with CALL and POP just before
                 the timed block.  Cog runs must read the cog address of the
                 POP, hub runs the hub address of the POP (at or above $400).
                 Every run reads its site word back and it must be the case's
                 instruction.
    Measure      hub SKIPF, pattern, five repeats.
  S_TOL is the slack around each timed reading.  The two timed readings are
  the measured saving apart, and the saving must exceed twice S_TOL, so no
  time can fall in both.  S_TOL is one clock, less than the two clocks of one
  instruction, so a run one instruction away from a reading is not that
  reading.

  READINGS, from the five hub SKIPF runs:
    REVERTS TO SKIP  sum 321 every time, and every time within S_TOL clocks of
                     the hub SKIP time; instructions were cancelled
    LEAPS            sum 321 every time, and every time within S_TOL clocks of
                     the hub SKIP time less the saving the cog control measured
    NO EFFECT        sum 511 every time; the pattern was not applied
    OTHER            sum 321 at any other time, or one other sum, printed raw
    MIXED            the sums did not all agree; the run lines are the raw values
    NO READING       a premise or a control above missed, or a run did not finish

NOT MEASURED
  REP or a nested REP in hub execution, a nested REP that ends on the outer
  block's last instruction, a nested REP of a single instruction, a count of 0.
  EXECF, SKIPF under other patterns, a SKIPF whose first instruction is
  skipped, more than seven skipped in a row, SKIPF over a branch.  One part,
  N = 1.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001

  STEP_MS         = 200                 ' a worker unfinished by then is reported
  DONE_V          = $600D_0001
  SENT            = $DEAD_BEEF          ' a record field no worker wrote

  ' record fields shared by both arms
  F_DONE          = 0
  F_MODE          = 1
  F_P1            = 2                   ' arm S: hub address of the body
  F_P2            = 3                   ' arm S: hub address of the site
  REC_N           = 10

  ' arm R
  NR_OUT          = 5                   ' passes of the outer REP
  NR_INN          = 3                   ' passes of the inner REP
  NR_BOTH         = NR_OUT * NR_INN
  N_R             = 3                   ' repeats of each case
  CR_OUT          = 0                   ' outer only, mode %01
  CR_INN          = 1                   ' inner only, mode %10
  CR_BTH          = 2                   ' both, mode %11
  CR_CASES        = 3
  FR_PRE          = 4
  FR_IN1          = 5
  FR_IN2          = 6
  FR_POST         = 7
  FR_OW           = 8                   ' site O word, read back
  FR_IW           = 9                   ' site I word, read back

  ' arm S
  N_S             = 5                   ' repeats of each case
  PAT_V           = %1011_1110          ' ADDs 1, 7 and 9 run
  SUM_PAT         = 1 + 64 + 256
  SUM_ALL         = 511
  S_TOL           = 1                   ' clocks, under one instruction; see the rig notes
  SC_CS           = 0                   ' cog SKIP, pattern
  SC_CF           = 1                   ' cog SKIPF, pattern
  SC_C0           = 2                   ' cog SKIPF, zero pattern
  SC_HS           = 3                   ' hub SKIP, pattern
  SC_H0           = 4                   ' hub SKIP, zero pattern
  SC_HF           = 5                   ' hub SKIPF, pattern: the case under test
  SC_CASES        = 6
  FS_SUM          = 4
  FS_CLK          = 5
  FS_PC           = 6                   ' the PC the body captured
  FS_XPC          = 7                   ' cog runs: the cog address of the POP
  FS_WORD         = 8                   ' site word, read back
  FS_PROG         = 9                   ' how far the run got
  PROG_IN         = 1                   ' about to enter the body
  PROG_PC         = 2                   ' the body captured its PC
  PROG_END        = 3                   ' the body finished
  HUB_MIN         = $400                ' the lowest hub-execution address
  COG_TOP         = $200                ' above every cog address the body uses

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long  recR[CR_CASES * N_R * REC_N]
  long  rOk[CR_CASES * N_R]
  long  recS[SC_CASES * N_S * REC_N]
  long  sOk[SC_CASES * N_S]

PUB main()
'' Run arms R and S and print every reading and verdict.
''

  p0(string("=== test-contract-gaps-p4-rep-skipf ==="))
  run_r()
  report_r()
  run_s()
  report_s()
  p0(string("=== END ==="))
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- the rig

PRI launch(pImg, pRec, mode, p1v, p2v) : ok | cog, t0
' Run one step in a fresh worker cog and wait for its DONE.
'
' @param pImg - hub address of the worker image
' @param pRec - hub address of the step's record
' @param mode - the step's mode word
' @param p1v - first hub address the step needs
' @param p2v - second hub address the step needs
' @returns ok - TRUE when the worker wrote DONE in time

' Local Variables:
' @local cog - the worker cog
' @local t0 - CT at the launch

  longfill(pRec, SENT, REC_N)
  long[pRec][F_DONE] := 0
  long[pRec][F_MODE] := mode
  long[pRec][F_P1] := p1v
  long[pRec][F_P2] := p2v
  cog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, pImg, pRec)
  if cog < 0
    p0(string("RIG FAIL: no free cog for a step"))
    return FALSE
  t0 := getct()
  repeat until long[pRec][F_DONE] == DONE_V
    if getct() - t0 > clkfreq / 1000 * STEP_MS
      cogstop(cog)
      p1(string("STEP HUNG: no DONE within the step limit, mode"), mode)
      return FALSE
  cogstop(cog)
  ok := TRUE

PRI rrec(k, i) : pr
' Find one arm R record.
'
' @param k - the case
' @param i - the repeat
' @returns pr - hub address of the record

  pr := @recR[(k * N_R + i) * REC_N]

PRI srec(k, i) : pr
' Find one arm S record.
'
' @param k - the case
' @param i - the repeat
' @returns pr - hub address of the record

  pr := @recS[(k * N_S + i) * REC_N]

PRI s_modeof(k) : m
' Map an arm S case to its mode word.
'
' @param k - the case
' @returns m - bit 0 SKIPF, bit 1 zero pattern, bit 2 hub

  m := lookupz(k: %000, %001, %011, %100, %110, %101)

PRI s_is_hub(k) : yes
' Whether an arm S case runs from hub.
'
' @param k - the case
' @returns yes - TRUE when it does

  yes := (s_modeof(k) & %100) <> 0

PRI run_r() | k, i
' Run every case of arm R.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local k - the case
' @local i - the repeat

  repeat k from 0 to CR_CASES - 1
    repeat i from 0 to N_R - 1
      rOk[k * N_R + i] := launch(@r_entry, rrec(k, i), k + 1, 0, 0)

PRI run_s() | k, i
' Run every case of arm S.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local k - the case
' @local i - the repeat

  repeat k from 0 to SC_CASES - 1
    repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
      sOk[k * N_S + i] := launch(@s_entry, srec(k, i), s_modeof(k), @h_body, @h_site)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm R verdict

PRI r_match(pr, v0, v1, v2, v3) : yes
' Whether a run's counters are these values.
'
' @param pr - the record
' @param v0 - pre
' @param v1 - in1
' @param v2 - in2
' @param v3 - post
' @returns yes - TRUE when all four match

  yes := long[pr][FR_PRE] == v0 and long[pr][FR_IN1] == v1 and long[pr][FR_IN2] == v2 and long[pr][FR_POST] == v3

PRI r_ok_runs() : ok | k, i, pr, xo, xi
' Whether every run finished with the site words its case needs.
'
' @returns ok - TRUE when they did

' Local Variables:
' @local k - the case
' @local i - the repeat
' @local pr - the record
' @local xo - the site O word this case needs
' @local xi - the site I word this case needs

  repeat k from 0 to CR_CASES - 1
    xo := ((k + 1) & 1) ? long[@r_to] : 0
    xi := ((k + 1) & 2) ? long[@r_ti] : 0
    repeat i from 0 to N_R - 1
      pr := rrec(k, i)
      if not rOk[k * N_R + i]
        return FALSE
      if long[pr][FR_OW] <> xo or long[pr][FR_IW] <> xi
        return FALSE
  ok := TRUE

PRI r_ctl(k, v0, v1, v2, v3) : ok | i
' Whether every repeat of a control read these values.
'
' @param k - the case
' @param v0 - pre
' @param v1 - in1
' @param v2 - in2
' @param v3 - post
' @returns ok - TRUE when they all did

' Local Variables:
' @local i - the repeat

  repeat i from 0 to N_R - 1
    if not r_match(rrec(k, i), v0, v1, v2, v3)
      return FALSE
  ok := TRUE

PRI r_reached() : ok | i, pr
' Whether every run under test reached the inner REP's slot and went past it.
'
' @returns ok - TRUE when they did

' Local Variables:
' @local i - the repeat
' @local pr - the record

  repeat i from 0 to N_R - 1
    pr := rrec(CR_BTH, i)
    if long[pr][FR_PRE] < 1 or long[pr][FR_IN1] < 1
      return FALSE
  ok := TRUE

PRI report_r() | k, i, pr, same, pArm
' Print arm R's raw values, then its verdict from those values.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local k - the case
' @local i - the repeat
' @local pr - the record
' @local same - TRUE while every repeat under test matches the first
' @local pArm - the arm's name

  pArm := string("R REP inside REP")
  p0(string("R cases: 0 outer only, 1 inner only, 2 both"))
  p4(string("R outer REP word, inner REP word, outer passes, inner passes"), long[@r_to], long[@r_ti], NR_OUT, NR_INN)
  repeat k from 0 to CR_CASES - 1
    repeat i from 0 to N_R - 1
      pr := rrec(k, i)
      p4(string("R run: case, repeat, finished, pre"), k, i, rOk[k * N_R + i], long[pr][FR_PRE])
      p4(string("R run: in1, in2, post, site O word"), long[pr][FR_IN1], long[pr][FR_IN2], long[pr][FR_POST], long[pr][FR_OW])
      p1(string("R run: site I word"), long[pr][FR_IW])

  if not r_ok_runs()
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, a run did not finish or a site word is not the one its case needs"))
  elseif not r_ctl(CR_OUT, NR_OUT, NR_OUT, NR_OUT, NR_OUT)
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the outer-only control did not count 5 of each"))
  elseif not r_ctl(CR_INN, 1, NR_INN, NR_INN, 1)
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the inner-only control did not read 1, 3, 3, 1"))
  elseif not r_reached()
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the block did not reach the inner REP's slot in every run"))
  else
    pr := rrec(CR_BTH, 0)
    same := TRUE
    repeat i from 1 to N_R - 1
      if not r_match(rrec(CR_BTH, i), long[pr][FR_PRE], long[pr][FR_IN1], long[pr][FR_IN2], long[pr][FR_POST])
        same := FALSE
    if not same
      pv(pArm, string("MIXED, the repeats did not agree; the raw values are the run lines"))
    elseif r_match(pr, NR_OUT, NR_BOTH, NR_BOTH, NR_OUT)
      pv(pArm, string("NESTS, the outer block repeated and the inner REP repeated inside it"))
    elseif r_match(pr, 1, NR_INN, NR_INN, 1)
      pv(pArm, string("INNER REPLACES, the inner REP ran and the outer REP is gone"))
    elseif r_match(pr, NR_OUT, NR_OUT, NR_OUT, NR_OUT)
      pv(pArm, string("INNER IGNORED, the outer block repeated and the inner REP did nothing"))
    elseif r_match(pr, 1, 1, 1, 1)
      pv(pArm, string("BOTH CANCELLED, the block ran once and neither REP repeated"))
    else
      pv4(pArm, string("OTHER, pre, in1, in2, post"), long[pr][FR_PRE], long[pr][FR_IN1], long[pr][FR_IN2], long[pr][FR_POST])

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm S verdict

PRI s_xpc_of(k, pr) : xp
' The address a case's PC capture must read.
'
' @param k - the case
' @param pr - the record
' @returns xp - the hub or cog address of the POP

  if s_is_hub(k)
    xp := @h_pcm
  else
    xp := long[pr][FS_XPC]

PRI s_ok_runs(kFirst, kLast) : ok | k, i
' Whether every run of a span of cases finished and reached the end of its body.
'
' @param kFirst - the first case of the span
' @param kLast - the last case of the span
' @returns ok - TRUE when they did

' Local Variables:
' @local k - the case
' @local i - the repeat

  repeat k from kFirst to kLast
    repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
      if not sOk[k * N_S + i] or long[srec(k, i)][FS_PROG] <> PROG_END
        return FALSE
  ok := TRUE

PRI s_pc_ok() : ok | k, i, pr, xp
' Whether every run captured the PC of the memory its case runs from.
'
' @returns ok - TRUE when they did

' Local Variables:
' @local k - the case
' @local i - the repeat
' @local pr - the record
' @local xp - the address the capture must read

  if @h_pcm < HUB_MIN
    return FALSE
  repeat k from 0 to SC_CASES - 1
    repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
      pr := srec(k, i)
      xp := s_xpc_of(k, pr)
      if not s_is_hub(k) and (xp < 0 or xp >= COG_TOP)
        return FALSE
      if long[pr][FS_PC] <> xp
        return FALSE
  ok := TRUE

PRI s_word_ok() : ok | k, i, xw
' Whether every run read back the instruction its case needs at the site.
'
' @returns ok - TRUE when they did

' Local Variables:
' @local k - the case
' @local i - the repeat
' @local xw - the site word this case needs

  repeat k from 0 to SC_CASES - 1
    xw := (s_modeof(k) & 1) ? long[@s_t_skipf] : long[@s_t_skip]
    repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
      if long[srec(k, i)][FS_WORD] <> xw
        return FALSE
  ok := TRUE

PRI s_ctl_sum(k, xs) : ok | i
' Whether every repeat of a control summed to this value.
'
' @param k - the case
' @param xs - the expected sum
' @returns ok - TRUE when they all did

' Local Variables:
' @local i - the repeat

  repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
    if long[srec(k, i)][FS_SUM] <> xs
      return FALSE
  ok := TRUE

PRI s_lo(k) : v | i, x
' The smallest elapsed time of a case.
'
' @param k - the case
' @returns v - the lowest clock count

' Local Variables:
' @local i - the repeat
' @local x - one run's clocks

  v := POSX
  repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
    x := long[srec(k, i)][FS_CLK]
    if x < v
      v := x

PRI s_hi(k) : v | i, x
' The largest elapsed time of a case.
'
' @param k - the case
' @returns v - the highest clock count

' Local Variables:
' @local i - the repeat
' @local x - one run's clocks

  v := NEGX
  repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
    x := long[srec(k, i)][FS_CLK]
    if x > v
      v := x

PRI report_s() | k, i, pr, pArm, sum0, same, base, save, inC, inL, x
' Print arm S's raw values, then its verdict from those values.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local k - the case
' @local i - the repeat
' @local pr - the record
' @local pArm - the arm's name
' @local sum0 - the first hub SKIPF run's sum
' @local same - TRUE while every hub SKIPF sum matches the first
' @local base - the hub SKIP control's lowest time
' @local save - the clocks the cog control saved by leaping
' @local inC - every hub SKIPF time is within S_TOL of base
' @local inL - every hub SKIPF time is within S_TOL of base less save
' @local x - one run's clocks

  pArm := string("S SKIPF in hub")
  p0(string("S cases: 0 cog SKIP, 1 cog SKIPF, 2 cog SKIPF zero, 3 hub SKIP, 4 hub SKIP zero, 5 hub SKIPF"))
  p2(string("S SKIP word, SKIPF word"), long[@s_t_skip], long[@s_t_skipf])
  p3(string("S hub body, hub POP, hub site"), @h_body, @h_pcm, @h_site)
  repeat k from 0 to SC_CASES - 1
    repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
      pr := srec(k, i)
      p4(string("S run: case, repeat, finished, sum"), k, i, sOk[k * N_S + i], long[pr][FS_SUM])
      p4(string("S run: clocks, PC read, PC expected, site word"), long[pr][FS_CLK], long[pr][FS_PC], s_xpc_of(k, pr), long[pr][FS_WORD])
      p1(string("S run: progress (3 = finished)"), long[pr][FS_PROG])

  base := s_lo(SC_HS)
  save := s_lo(SC_CS) - s_lo(SC_CF)
  p4(string("S times: cog SKIP low, cog SKIPF low, saving, hub SKIP low"), s_lo(SC_CS), s_lo(SC_CF), save, base)
  p3(string("S times: hub SKIP high, hub SKIPF low, hub SKIPF high"), s_hi(SC_HS), s_lo(SC_HF), s_hi(SC_HF))

  if not s_ok_runs(SC_CS, SC_H0)
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, a control run did not finish; the progress lines show where"))
  elseif not s_ok_runs(SC_HF, SC_HF)
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the controls finished but a hub SKIPF run did not; the progress lines show where"))
  elseif not s_pc_ok()
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, a run's PC capture was not in the memory its case runs from"))
  elseif not s_word_ok()
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, a site word is not the instruction its case needs"))
  elseif not s_ctl_sum(SC_CS, SUM_PAT) or not s_ctl_sum(SC_CF, SUM_PAT)
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, a cog control under the pattern did not sum to 321"))
  elseif not s_ctl_sum(SC_C0, SUM_ALL)
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the cog zero-pattern control did not sum to 511"))
  elseif not s_ctl_sum(SC_HS, SUM_PAT)
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the hub SKIP control did not sum to 321"))
  elseif not s_ctl_sum(SC_H0, SUM_ALL)
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the hub zero-pattern control did not sum to 511"))
  elseif save <= 2 * S_TOL
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, cog SKIPF did not save enough clocks over cog SKIP to tell the readings apart"))
  elseif s_hi(SC_HS) - base > S_TOL
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, the hub SKIP control's times disagree by more than S_TOL"))
  else
    sum0 := long[srec(SC_HF, 0)][FS_SUM]
    same := TRUE
    repeat i from 1 to N_S - 1
      if long[srec(SC_HF, i)][FS_SUM] <> sum0
        same := FALSE
    if not same
      pv(pArm, string("MIXED, the hub SKIPF sums did not agree; the raw values are the run lines"))
    elseif sum0 == SUM_PAT
      inC := TRUE
      inL := TRUE
      repeat i from 0 to N_S - 1
        x := long[srec(SC_HF, i)][FS_CLK]
        if abs (x - base) > S_TOL
          inC := FALSE
        if abs (x - (base - save)) > S_TOL
          inL := FALSE
      if inC
        pv(pArm, string("REVERTS TO SKIP, the pattern was followed at the hub SKIP time"))
      elseif inL
        pv(pArm, string("LEAPS, the pattern was followed at the hub SKIP time less the saving"))
      else
        pv4(pArm, string("OTHER, the pattern was followed at another time: hub SKIP low, saving, SKIPF low, SKIPF high"), base, save, s_lo(SC_HF), s_hi(SC_HF))
    elseif sum0 == SUM_ALL
      pv(pArm, string("NO EFFECT, all nine ADDs ran; the pattern was not applied"))
    else
      pv1(pArm, string("OTHER, every hub SKIPF run summed to this one value"), sum0)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- printing

PRI p0(pS)
' Print a hub string.
'
' @param pS - the string

  debug(zstr_(pS))

PRI p1(pS, a)
' Print a hub string and one value.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - the value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a))

PRI p2(pS, a, b)
' Print a hub string and two values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b))

PRI p3(pS, a, b, c)
' Print a hub string and three values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value
' @param c - third value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b), " ", uhex_long_(c))

PRI p4(pS, a, b, c, d)
' Print a hub string and four values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value
' @param c - third value
' @param d - fourth value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b), " ", uhex_long_(c), " ", uhex_long_(d))

PRI pv(pArm, pText)
' Print one verdict line.
'
' @param pArm - the arm
' @param pText - the verdict

  debug("VERDICT ", zstr_(pArm), ": ", zstr_(pText))

PRI pv1(pArm, pText, v)
' Print one verdict line with its reading.
'
' @param pArm - the arm
' @param pText - the verdict
' @param v - the reading

  debug("VERDICT ", zstr_(pArm), ": ", zstr_(pText), " ", uhex_long_(v))

PRI pv4(pArm, pText, a, b, c, d)
' Print one verdict line with four readings.
'
' @param pArm - the arm
' @param pText - the verdict
' @param a - first reading
' @param b - second reading
' @param c - third reading
' @param d - fourth reading

  debug("VERDICT ", zstr_(pArm), ": ", zstr_(pText), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b), " ", uhex_long_(c), " ", uhex_long_(d))

DAT ' ---- arm R worker: runs in cog RAM ----
                alignl
                org     0
r_entry         rdlong  r_mode, ptra[F_MODE]
                testb   r_mode, #0      wc      ' bit 0: the outer REP is in place
        if_c    mov     r_osite, r_to
        if_nc   mov     r_osite, #0             ' the NOP word
                testb   r_mode, #1      wc      ' bit 1: the inner REP is in place
        if_c    mov     r_isite, r_ti
        if_nc   mov     r_isite, #0
                jmp     #r_osite                ' the branch clears the pipeline past the patches
r_osite         nop                             ' site O: REP #5,#NR_OUT or NOP
                add     r_pre, #1               ' outer body 1
r_isite         nop                             ' site I, outer body 2: REP #2,#NR_INN or NOP
                add     r_in1, #1               ' outer body 3, inner body 1
                add     r_in2, #1               ' outer body 4, inner body 2
                add     r_post, #1              ' outer body 5
                wrlong  r_pre, ptra[FR_PRE]
                wrlong  r_in1, ptra[FR_IN1]
                wrlong  r_in2, ptra[FR_IN2]
                wrlong  r_post, ptra[FR_POST]
                wrlong  r_osite, ptra[FR_OW]
                wrlong  r_isite, ptra[FR_IW]
                wrlong  r_donev, ptra[F_DONE]
                jmp     #$
r_to            rep     #5, #NR_OUT             ' copied into site O
r_ti            rep     #2, #NR_INN             ' copied into site I
r_donev         long    DONE_V
r_mode          long    0
r_pre           long    0
r_in1           long    0
r_in2           long    0
r_post          long    0

DAT ' ---- arm S worker: the cog side and the cog body ----
                alignl
                org     0
s_entry         rdlong  s_mode, ptra[F_MODE]
                rdlong  s_phub, ptra[F_P1]
                rdlong  s_psite, ptra[F_P2]
                testb   s_mode, #0      wc      ' bit 0: SKIPF
        if_c    mov     s_word, s_t_skipf
        if_nc   mov     s_word, s_t_skip
                testb   s_mode, #1      wc      ' bit 1: zero pattern
        if_nc   mov     s_pat, s_patv
        if_c    mov     s_pat, #0
                testb   s_mode, #2      wc      ' bit 2: run from hub
        if_c    jmp     #s_hubgo
                mov     s_site, s_word
                mov     s_rb, s_site
                mov     s_xpc, #s_pcm_c
                wrlong  #PROG_IN, ptra[FS_PROG]
                jmp     #s_body                 ' the branch clears the pipeline past the patch
s_hubgo         wrlong  s_word, s_psite         ' the site the hub body will run
                rdlong  s_rb, s_psite
                wrlong  #PROG_IN, ptra[FS_PROG]
                jmp     s_phub
s_body          call    #s_pcm_c
s_pcm_c         pop     s_pc
                and     s_pc, s_m20
                wrlong  s_pc, ptra[FS_PC]
                wrlong  #PROG_PC, ptra[FS_PROG]
                nop                             ' the same lead-in as the hub body
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                getct   s_t0
s_site          nop                             ' the site: SKIP or SKIPF, patched
                add     s_acc, #1
                add     s_acc, #2
                add     s_acc, #4
                add     s_acc, #8
                add     s_acc, #16
                add     s_acc, #32
                add     s_acc, #64
                add     s_acc, #128
                add     s_acc, #256
                getct   s_t1
s_report        sub     s_t1, s_t0
                wrlong  s_acc, ptra[FS_SUM]
                wrlong  s_t1, ptra[FS_CLK]
                wrlong  s_xpc, ptra[FS_XPC]
                wrlong  s_rb, ptra[FS_WORD]
                wrlong  #PROG_END, ptra[FS_PROG]
                wrlong  s_donev, ptra[F_DONE]
                jmp     #$
s_t_skip        skip    s_pat                   ' copied to the site
s_t_skipf       skipf   s_pat                   ' copied to the site
s_patv          long    PAT_V
s_m20           long    $F_FFFF
s_donev         long    DONE_V
s_mode          long    0
s_phub          long    0
s_psite         long    0
s_word          long    0
s_pat           long    0
s_acc           long    0
s_t0            long    0
s_t1            long    0
s_pc            long    0
s_xpc           long    0
s_rb            long    0

' ---- arm S worker: the hub body ----
                orgh
                alignl
h_body          call    #h_pcm
h_pcm           pop     s_pc
                and     s_pc, s_m20
                wrlong  s_pc, ptra[FS_PC]
                wrlong  #PROG_PC, ptra[FS_PROG]
                nop                             ' lets the FIFO get ahead before the timed part
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                getct   s_t0
h_site          nop                             ' the site: SKIP or SKIPF, written by the worker
                add     s_acc, #1
                add     s_acc, #2
                add     s_acc, #4
                add     s_acc, #8
                add     s_acc, #16
                add     s_acc, #32
                add     s_acc, #64
                add     s_acc, #128
                add     s_acc, #256
                getct   s_t1
                jmp     #\s_report
